+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+<meta charset="UTF-8">
+<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
+<title>BIO 004 Human Anatomy &middot; Fall 2026 &middot; Course Home</title>
+<link rel="canonical" href="welcome.html">
+<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
+
+<!--
+  ============================================================
+  BIO 004 Human Anatomy, Fall 2026
+  canvas-home.html
+
+  REDIRECT. The real front door is welcome.html.
+
+  This briefly existed as its own front door with a "set up your
+  course" step and an Enter Course screen. It was retired because
+  welcome.html already does that job and does it better: the
+  greeting, the aurora, the section picker, the walkthrough, the
+  welcome-back screen and the module and week hubgate are all
+  there and all designed as one piece.
+
+  Kept as a redirect rather than deleted so any Canvas page,
+  bookmark or link already pointing here keeps working. If nothing
+  points at it, this file is safe to delete.
+
+  THE CANVAS IFRAME SHOULD POINT AT welcome.html.
+
+  Redirect order matters. The meta refresh is the fallback; the
+  script runs first and uses replace() so this page does not land
+  in the student's back-button history and trap them bouncing
+  between the two. Any ?sec= or ?frameId= parameters are carried
+  across, because dropping them would lose the section a link was
+  trying to set.
+  ============================================================
+-->
+
+<meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url=welcome.html">
+
+<style>
+  body{margin:0;font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',system-ui,sans-serif;
+       background:#08101F;color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;
+       justify-content:center;min-height:100vh;text-align:center;padding:24px}
+  a{color:#DCB45C;font-weight:700}
+</style>
+</head>
+<body>
+
+<p>
+  Taking you to the course home.<br>
+  <a href="welcome.html" target="_top">Continue to BIO 004 Human Anatomy</a>
+</p>
+
+<script>
+(function () {
+  'use strict';
+  var q = '';
+  try { q = location.search || ''; } catch (e) {}
+  try {
+    location.replace('welcome.html' + q);
+  } catch (e) {
+    location.href = 'welcome.html' + q;
+  }
+})();
+</script>
+
+</body>
+</html>
